# The negative variants of probe-tests/widgets/navigation.probe: every test below asserts something WRONG, and every one must FAIL.
# They show that the positive suite can fail, and why. This file does not end in .probe, so `probe test` never picks it up in a directory run. To run it:
#
#   cp probe-tests/negative/navigation.probe.expect-fail /tmp/navigation-negative.probe
#   probe test /tmp/navigation-negative.probe --device <serial> -y       # (the navigation build, the same probe.yaml as for navigation.probe)
#
# Expected: 0 passed, 5 failed, each with the message in its comment. A test that passes is a finding: either the agent changed or the positive suite no longer proves what it says.
# Each test must fail at its own step, with the message in its comment. A failure at the `wait until` of `before each test` (a timeout
# waiting for the screen's last element) is NOT the expected failure: the screen never showed, and the run proves nothing.

before each test
  restart the app
  # Right after a restart the agent can answer while the screen is still being built (issue #793): wait for the screen's last element
  # with an id. `wait until ... appears` matches only what is on screen, so this needs a screen tall enough to show that element
  # (measured on a Pixel 6 profile); on a shorter one the wait would time out. A wait for an earlier element was not enough (measured).
  wait until #wf_open_message appears

# Expected: see "Inbox": Expected to see "text("Inbox")" but it was not found (the first route is under the opaque message route)
test "N1 the route under the top one is seen"
  see "Inbox"
  tap "Open message"
  wait until "From: Ada" appears
  see "Inbox"

# Expected: see "Queries: 2": ... was not found (one tap on the action is one search)
test "N2 one tap on the action counts twice"
  tap "Search"
  see "Queries: 2"

# Expected: see "From: Ada": ... was not found (no route was pushed)
test "N3 the second route before it is pushed"
  see "From: Ada"

# Expected: see "From: Ada": ... was not found (go back popped the message route)
test "N4 the message route after go back"
  tap "Open message"
  wait until "From: Ada" appears
  go back
  wait until "From: Ada" disappears
  see "From: Ada"

# Expected: tap "Serch": Widget not found: text("Serch") — visible texts: [...]
test "N5 a tooltip that is not on the screen"
  tap "Serch"
